-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Inferno
  Publisher   Proxima Software, 1993
  Version     1.2

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Inferno.tzx
  MD5         335eec35a526f2044455cb87e8c77206

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). The game's own code
  plays unchanged; the build adds a Kempston default at play start and keeps
  pilots in INFERNO.SAV on the SD card.

  Changes     1.2: loading screen (the game's title picture) from ENTER; cheat
              toggles Infinite fuel and Infinite ammo. 1.1: Kempston joystick
              works; pilot SAVE and LOAD go to INFERNO.SAV on the SD card,
              with an autosave at each mission start; English briefing title
              pictures and attract-mode credits (MUSIC, GRAPHICS); no Czech
              flash before an English briefing. 1.0: first NXC patch, from
              nexclash inferno hybrid build with English text; Czech as the
              language set

  Note        The whole game from the tape (intro, six levels, ending) with
              the figures as Next hardware sprites over a tilemap scenery; the
              original code runs, with small hooks for the joystick, the saves
              and the cheats. Needs a 2MB Next. English by default (a reviewed
              translation: menus, intro, briefings and their title pictures,
              story, debriefs, credits, command words HELP KEY REP WEA QUI
              PAS); the Language line gives the original Czech. Kempston:
              answer Y (A in Czech) at the prompt; weapon and activate stay on
              Symbol Shift and N. Pilots: SAVE and LOAD use INFERNO.SAV in the
              game's folder on the SD card (112 pilots, names in either case),
              and the pilot is saved by itself at each mission start; with no
              card they stay in RAM. Loading screen: the game's title picture,
              from ENTER. Cheats: Infinite fuel, Infinite ammo. Never run
              automap_fix or any DivMMC automap-off step on this build: the
              saves call esxDOS.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Toggle  Infinite fuel
  Toggle  Infinite ammo

  The Tipshop's Multiface POKEs for this game (Viktor Drozd), read in the
  game's unpacked code: fuel 44519,0 + 37103,0 and ammo 44919,0 are DEC made
  NOP. Its energy POKE 44492,0 is left out: it is not a DEC but the high byte
  of LD A,(44105), so it makes a test read ROM at 0049, which the Next build
  pages differently. The code is packed on the tape, so the cheats are build
  toggles that make the change once the game has unpacked it, not POKEs.

